      "id": 1,
      "text": "Muscatine began as a trading post founded by Colonel George Davenport’s representatives in 1833.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muscatine%2C_Iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By the turn of the century, Muscatine was the world’s largest pearl button manufacturer, earning the nickname Pearl Button Capital of the World.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.muscatineiowa.gov/341/Muscatine-History"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first passenger train ran between Davenport and Muscatine on November 20, 1855, marking the city’s arrival on the railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.muscatineiowa.gov/341/Muscatine-History"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The National Pearl Button Museum at the History and Industry Center lets visitors explore the city’s button‑making heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.traveliowa.com/cities/muscatine-iowa/659/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Muscatine’s early industry was dominated by lumbering, saw and planing mills, and sash and door factories that shaped the town’s growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
